+<Param name="model" type="'longpipe' | 'mediapipe-selfie' | …" default="'longpipe'">
+
+Which segmentation model runs inside the pipeline. Everything else — the worker, frame transport, WebGPU / WebGL2 backends, zero-copy input and the compositor — is the same either way.
+
+```ts
+new EffectsPipeline(stream, { model: 'mediapipe-selfie', background: 'blur' })
+```
+
+- `'longpipe'` (default): Longpipe's own models (five tiers, see [Presets](/docs/presets)). Every effect: backgrounds, touch-up, auto-reframe, optical-flow temporal stabilization.
+- `'mediapipe-selfie'`: Google's [MediaPipe Selfie Segmenter](/docs/models#mediapipe-selfie). **Background effects only.** The square (256×256) or landscape (256×144) variant is picked from the output aspect ratio; `'mediapipe-selfie-square'` / `'mediapipe-selfie-landscape'` force one.
+
+With a MediaPipe model, `touchup`, `reframe` and any `preset` other than `'auto'` **throw at construction** (`…requires a Longpipe model; set model: 'longpipe'`), as do `setTouchup()`, `setReframe()`, `reframe()` and `setPreset()` later. Autotune and the adaptive controller don't run. See [Models](/docs/models).
+
+</Param>
