+### MediaPipe selfie weights
+
+If you use [`model: 'mediapipe-selfie'`](/docs/models#mediapipe-selfie), host these two files in the **same folder** as everything else (the SDK fetches them from `weightsBaseUrl` when you set it):
+
+- `mediapipe_selfie_segmenter.f16.bin` (square, 256×256)
+- `mediapipe_selfie_segmenter_landscape.f16.bin` (landscape, 256×144)
+
+You only need the variant(s) you use: `'mediapipe-selfie'` picks landscape for 16:9-ish output and square otherwise. Download them from `https://cdn.longpipe.dev/models/mediapipe/selfie/v1/`, which also has `manifest.json` (sizes and sha256), `LICENSE` and `NOTICE.md`, or regenerate them from Google's original `.tflite` files with [`scripts/convert_mediapipe_selfie.py`](https://github.com/sb2702/longpipe/blob/main/scripts/convert_mediapipe_selfie.py). These weights are Google's, under **Apache-2.0**: keep the `LICENSE` and `NOTICE.md` alongside them when you redistribute.
+
+Without `weightsBaseUrl`, MediaPipe weights come from `https://cdn.longpipe.dev/models/mediapipe/selfie/v1/` (versioned separately from Longpipe's own weights, since they only change if Google's model does).
